  "label": "Harmful",
  "description": "The meme weaponizes the image of Martin Luther King Jr. to frame a political decision as a personal, existential choice, potentially undermining the legacy of MLK and reducing complex political discourse to a simplistic, emotionally charged statement. The juxtaposition of the serious historical figure with the absurdity of 'leaving the country' creates a tone of performative outrage that can be seen as disrespectful to the civil rights movement and its leaders. The meme also encourages engagement ('like and share') based on a potentially divisive political stance, which can amplify polarization and misinformation.",
